        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/858c86/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-17T21:18:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MarioFanaticXV\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/48/2129_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MarioFanaticXV:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Okay, I took a scan of my Wraith card… If I'm understanding Chromium_Man, this is what he's referring to:&nbsp;<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/75RhIIn.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Large Image link</a>I'm not used to this scanner yet, so I cut off a bit of the card, but there's more than enough that you can see what I think we're talking about.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This is exactly what I mean. &nbsp;I called them Kirby dots as a little comic book homage, but they're really just minor printing errors. &nbsp;I have them relatively badly on my Ra panel, and much more minor on my Tachyon and Unity panels. &nbsp;</p>",
